<p><span>Acne is a common skin condition that occurs when hair follicles become clogged with oil and dead skin cells. Struggling with breakouts, blemishes or hormonal acne?  </span></p>
<p><span>We all deserve to feel our best. </span></p>

<p>Acne typically appears on the face, neck, chest, back, and shoulders, where oil glands are more prevalent. It often leads to the formation of pimples, whiteheads, blackheads, and sometimes deeper, painful cysts or nodules. Acne can affect people of all ages and can be influenced by factors such as genetics, hormonal fluctuations, stress, certain medications, and dietary habits.</p>
<p>Understanding the cause of your acne is key to finding your path to clear, radiant skin. Don’t let acne hold you back – reclaim your confidence and embrace your journey to healthier, happier skin.</p>
<p>Treatment for acne may involve topical creams or gels, oral medications such as the contraceptive pill, lifestyle changes, and skincare routines aimed at reducing oil production, unclogging pores, and preventing inflammation.</p>
<p><strong>Our Partner Doctors are here to assist you with the medication you need for acne treatment.</strong></p>
